{
 "lesson": {
  "schema_version": "1.5",
  "title": "Why a projectile flies farthest at 45 degrees",
  "steps": [
   {
    "id": "s1",
    "script": "With no air resistance, equal launch and landing heights, and fixed launch speed, forty-five degrees gives the greatest horizontal range. Let's see why.",
    "ops": [
     {
      "op": "text",
      "id": "title",
      "region": "A1",
      "content": "Why launch at 45\u00b0?"
     },
     {
      "op": "text",
      "id": "conditions",
      "anchor": {
       "el": "title",
       "side": "below",
       "gap": 0.08
      },
      "content": "Same speed; level ground; no air drag"
     },
     {
      "op": "figure",
      "id": "flight",
      "region": "right",
      "frame": {
       "x": [
        -0.5,
        11
       ],
       "y": [
        -0.6,
        5
       ],
       "axes": "edge",
       "equal_scale": true,
       "x_label": "Horizontal distance (m)",
       "y_label": "Height (m)"
      },
      "marks": [
       {
        "kind": "fn",
        "id": "path45",
        "y": "x-x^2/10",
        "domain": [
         0,
         10
        ],
        "label": "45\u00b0"
       },
       {
        "kind": "point",
        "id": "launch",
        "at": [
         0,
         0
        ]
       },
